## Context
Part of #20921: scroll performance batch 1

## Problem
`MessageCellView.==` (line 1700) does a nested `zip().allSatisfy()` over `providerCatalog` arrays — O(providers × models) per cell per body evaluation. The catalog rarely changes (only on settings update), so this is wasted work.

## Implementation
1. Add a `providerCatalogHash: Int` stored property to `MessageCellView` (alongside `providerCatalog` at line 1742).
2. Where `MessageCellView` is constructed in the `ForEach` (around line 995), compute the hash from the catalog and pass it.
3. In `MessageCellView.==`, replace the nested zip (line 1700) with `lhs.providerCatalogHash == rhs.providerCatalogHash`.
4. Add a helper function to compute the hash:
```swift
private static func hashCatalog(_ catalog: [ProviderCatalogEntry]) -> Int {
    var hasher = Hasher()
    for entry in catalog {
        hasher.combine(entry.id)
        hasher.combine(entry.displayName)
        for model in entry.models {
            hasher.combine(model.id)
            hasher.combine(model.displayName)
        }
    }
    return hasher.finalize()
}
```

